All 48 pages listed in `_source-lists/de_chunk_00` were fetched and archived as markdown under `reference/pages/de/` (mirroring URL path hierarchy, e.g. `reference/pages/de/branchen/automotive.md`).

## Notes on borderline cases (not counted as failures)
- `https://www.dietz.eu/46-2/` → `reference/pages/de/46-2.md` — WebFetch returned no real page title or heading structure; content was almost entirely nav/footer/certification badges (numeric slug suggests a stub/legacy WordPress page ID). Documented in the file with a note; not a fetch error, just thin/uncertain content worth a manual spot-check later.
- `https://www.dietz.eu/blog/` → `reference/pages/de/blog.md` — is a paginated index/listing page; WebFetch truncated the full 50+ entry enumeration, so the file captures a representative sample of entries rather than the exhaustive list (most individual articles are separately archived as their own pages anyway).
- `https://www.dietz.eu/beispiel-seite/` → `reference/pages/de/beispiel-seite.md` — default unmodified WordPress sample page, documented as such.

## Images
Total unique image URLs referenced across all 48 pages: 123
Missing/undownloaded: 0 (all 123 verified present as local files under `reference/assets/images/` — deduplicated against the whole assets/images tree, including images already fetched by other chunks/locales, e.g. `assets/images/en/`, so many were skip-as-existing rather than freshly downloaded in this run).
No image download failures encountered in this chunk (one transient issue with `aeo.png` on the `relaunch.dietz.eu` host was resolved by re-fetching the same filename from `www.dietz.eu`, which mirrors the same media library).

## Rate limiting note
WebFetch hit shared HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests) rate limits on the dietz.eu domain multiple times during this run (likely due to concurrent crawl activity from other chunk-processing sessions hitting the same host). Each time, a short cooldown followed by a retry resolved it — no URLs were skipped or given up on because of this.
